  "limitations": [
    "Only seeds 1000..1011, single day-6 interval. The 32-pair 30-day batch is not evaluated by this report.",
    "Mortal use increases in 10/12 pairs, with two regressions; aggregate improvement is not universal or a survival result.",
    "Mortal actor plus mortal author does not prove independence from protected teachers, transfers, care or other intermediaries.",
    "Recipe teaching events omit recipeId; the displayed recipe name is not a reliable identity. Historical teaching-to-use linkage cannot be reconstructed.",
    "learnedFrom is endpoint-local, removed on forgetting and absent from deceased legacy. The existing learned-use count omits those histories and <=tick does not establish within-tick order.",
    "Teaching classification uses literal causes tied to the frozen source revisions; missing or pruned coverage must be unknown, not zero.",
    "This is poststratification with separately hashed queries, not a retroactive change to the frozen metricsVersion2 instrument."
  ],
  "recommendedFutureContract": [
    "Keep global metrics descriptive; publish mortal, protected and unknown strata plus actor/author and teacher/learner matrices with explicit intervals and a new instrument version.",
    "For causal teaching-to-use attribution persist structured recipeId, teacherId, learnerId, tick and executionCounterBefore at teaching. Require later tick or later execution serial within same tick; use EXISTS or one latest relevant lesson to avoid duplicated use counts.",
    "Persist learning receipts independently from local forgetting/death; never infer recipe identity from display names."
  ],
  "recommendedTests": [
    "Real Store: use then death before save remains in mortal use totals.",
    "Mortal-invented tool used by protected actor and protected-invented tool used by mortal remain different cells.",
    "Unknown actor/author, failed/non-use/zero-benefit and interval boundaries remain explicit.",
    "Forgetting and teacher/learner death do not delete durable learning evidence.",
    "Same-tick use before/after teaching and repeated teaching count only causally subsequent uses once.",
    "Generic learning habits and duplicate learning/cooperation receipts are not counted as extra recipe transmissions; pruned/missing history produces unknown."
